The token is sent with each request and kept nowhere else; nothing here logs it.

## Use

```python
from {{ package }} import Twin

with Twin() as twin:
{%- if example_type %}
    first = twin.{{ example_type.attribute }}.list(limit=10)         # typed models, at head
    earlier = twin.{{ example_type.attribute }}.list(at="#1")        # as of an earlier version
    one = twin.{{ example_type.attribute }}.get(first[0].uid)
    edges = twin.{{ example_type.attribute }}.links(one.uid)
    changes = twin.{{ example_type.attribute }}.history(one.uid)
    table = twin.{{ example_type.attribute }}.table()               # a pyarrow.Table
{%- endif %}
{%- if example_question %}
    answer = twin.questions.{{ example_question.method }}()
    print(answer.value, answer.unit)
{%- endif %}
```

Every read is of one version of the twin: `at` is `head` (the default), a commit
id, `#<seq>` or an ISO 8601 time with an offset (the last version at or before it).
A refused request raises `TwinApiError` with the API's status and problem code.

